---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Academic Audit

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10  
**Integration calibration:** Class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]` — Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test severities downgraded per calibration rules.

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4** (of 8)   |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic (testsmells.org)  
**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)  
**Risk:** The `if/else` means only one branch ever executes per run — the other path is silently untested.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — one assertion branch is always hidden
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two tests with deterministic setup:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(((PremiumUser)loaded).DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Unknown Test / Empty Test (testsmells.org)  
**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)  
**Risk:** Test passes as long as no exception is thrown — a silently broken `Insert` that writes garbage data would never be caught.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion; "passes" even if Insert is a no-op
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test (testsmells.org)  
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)  
**Calibration:** Downgraded from High → Medium because this is an integration test, but `Thread.Sleep(3000)` is still a smell — it makes the suite 3 s slower and is timing-dependent.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — hard-coded 3-second wall-clock wait
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout instead of a fixed sleep:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll up to 5 s, checking every 100 ms
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
    {
        Assert.IsTrue(DateTime.UtcNow < deadline, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
}
```

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette (testsmells.org extended catalog)  
**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)  
**Risk:** Four assertions with no message parameters — when one fails, the runner reports only "Assert.AreEqual failed" with no indication of *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 bare assertions
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add a message to each assertion:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining 4 tests are well-structured:

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion on the expected absence |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | `Assert.AreEqual(3, ...)` is contextually obvious (3 items just added) — not a Magic Number smell |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency test with a clear assertion |

The `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` fixture is tight — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test, so **General Fixture** does not apply.

---

### Smells Not Detected (15 of 19 clean)

Mystery Guest, Eager Test, Magic Number Test, Sensitive Equality, Exception Handling, General Fixture, Ignored Test, Duplicate Assert, Lazy Test, Constructor Initialization, Default Test, Redundant Print, Redundant Assertion, Resource Optimism, Empty Test — **all clean**.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, …)` after bulk insert | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 deterministic tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop | ~5 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to 4 assertions | ~2 min |

Items 1–2 prevent **false-pass risk** (tests that pass when they shouldn't) and should be fixed first. Items 3–4 improve reliability and diagnostics.
